    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION If\nyou invest in our Common Stock in this offering, you will experience immediate and substantial dilution in the as adjusted net tangible\nbook value of your shares of Common Stock. Dilution in as adjusted net tangible book value represents the difference between the assumed\nprice to the public per share of our Common Stock and the as adjusted net tangible book value per share of our Common Stock immediately\nfollowing this offering. Pro forma net tangible book value per share\nrepresents our total tangible assets (total assets less intangible assets) less total liabilities, divided by the outstanding shares\nof Common Stock. As of June 30, 2026, our net tangible book value was ($29,533), or ($0.31) per share, based on 96,791,416 pro forma\nshares of common stock outstanding, (which gives effect to the reclassification of 500,000 shares of common stock remaining unissued\npursuant to",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
